// Every text of NSW-Home's menu in every language: one line per Spanish text (see lang.h).
//
//   F("<Spanish>", "<file>/<label>")
//       The console has this row or message: its wording is read from the firmware at runtime,
//       in the chosen language, from message/<folder>/<file>.msbt in the HOME Menu (or another
//       system applet, see fwtext.cpp). Only the id is here. A Spanish text with %1..%9 in it
//       is a pattern (%#1: a part that is only digits); the message's values (its date, version... tags) go in those places, in
//       the order they come in the console's Spanish text.
//   O("<Spanish>", en-US, en-GB, fr, fr-CA, de, it, es-419, ja, ko, zh-Hans, zh-Hant, nl, pt, pt-BR, ru)
//       Our own translation (UTF-8, like every text here). "" takes the other region's column (en-GB <- en-US, fr-CA <- fr,
//       pt-BR <- pt) and, for es-419, the Spanish itself. A line can stand beside an F line for
//       the same text: it is what is shown when there is no firmware to read.
//   K("<text>")
//       The same in every language (a name): never reported as missing.
//
// To add a string: copy a line of the right kind, keep it in its group. `tools/lang_missing.py`
// lists the texts drawn on screen that have no line here.

